From 81bc450792011c9bf8cbba40d9172c7bbfbaa222 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonny Heggheim <hegjon@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 07:20:02 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 01/12] libalpm: read btrpkg indexes and their signatures

btrpkg (https://github.com/hegjon/btrpkg) stores a package as an index (header,
chunk table, entries, small-file blob) plus chunks that btrfs can take as
compressed extents. btrpkg.c parses and checks a format version 0 index (the
version stays 0 while the format is unstable) the way btrpkg's own reader
does (same checks, same verdict on crafted input) and verifies its
signify-format Ed25519 signature over the 256-byte header with OpenSSL,
against *.pub keys minus a 'revoked' list.

Built when the crypto provider is OpenSSL and libzstd is found (HAVE_BTRPKG).
Nothing calls it yet. test/btrpkg: btrdump prints the parsed index in the same
text form as 'btrpkg dump'; run.sh checks a real index and signature, every bit
flip and cut, and crafted indexes with valid hashes and bad contents.
